# SEO, AEO, and GEO

Playbook with examples: `docs/seo-aeo-geo.md`. Google guidance: https://developers.google.com/search/docs/ and https://developers.google.com/search/docs/appearance/ai-features

## Every page

- Unique `title` (10-70 characters, page name first, site name appended by `BaseLayout`) and `description` (50-160 characters, a plain summary that would make sense as a search snippet).
- Canonical URL is generated from `Astro.site` + pathname. Override only for intentional duplicates.
- One `h1`. Headings form an outline a reader could skim. Important content is HTML text, not text inside images.
- Internal links: each page links to its parent (services hub), at least one sibling or related page, and a contact path. Link text describes the target ("WordPress development services", not "click here").
- Open Graph title, description, and type come from `BaseLayout`; pass `ogImage` once a social image exists.
- `noindex` only for thank-you and utility pages. Draft content is never built.
- `robots.txt` allows crawling and points at `sitemap-index.xml` (generated by `@astrojs/sitemap` from `site` in `astro.config.mjs`).

## Structured data (JSON-LD)

Render JSON-LD through components in `src/components/seo/` with typed props, injected via the `head` slot. Only mark up what is visible on the page.

| Page | Types |
| --- | --- |
| Home | `Organization` (name, url, logo when available, `sameAs` for real profiles only) and `WebSite` |
| Service pages | `Service` with `provider` referencing the Organization, plus `BreadcrumbList` |
| Case studies | `CreativeWork` or `Article` with `about`, plus `BreadcrumbList` |
| Insights articles | `Article` (headline, datePublished, dateModified, author as Organization or Person) |
| About | `AboutPage` with the Organization |
| Contact | `ContactPage` |

- `FAQPage` markup is allowed only where each question and answer is visible on the page. Google stopped showing FAQ rich results in May 2026, so do not expect a search appearance from it; keep it when the content is genuinely a FAQ because other engines and assistants may read it.
- Do not add `AggregateRating`, `Review`, or award markup without real, verifiable data.
- The JSON must parse; `tests/e2e/seo.spec.ts` fails on invalid JSON-LD.

## Answer engine optimisation (AEO)

- Open each service page, article, and FAQ answer with a direct answer in one or two sentences, then details.
- Use question-style `h2`/`h3` headings for sections that answer a question. Keep each answer self-contained so it can be quoted alone.
- Add a short FAQ section (from the `faqs` collection) to service pages where real questions exist. Define terms the audience may not know (AEO, GEO, lifecycle email) in one sentence when first used.

## Generative engine optimisation (GEO)

- State who Auralink Studio is, what it does, and for whom in plain text on the home and about pages, consistent with `src/data/site.ts`. Keep name, services, and contact details identical everywhere they appear.
- Give articles a visible author or organisation attribution and dates. Cite sources for any statistic with a link.
- Google states no special files or markup are required for AI features; the requirements are indexability, helpful people-first content, and structured data that matches visible content. Do not add fabricated "AI summary" blocks or hidden text.
- Keep pages crawlable: no content behind client-side-only rendering; islands enhance, they do not own primary content.

## Not allowed

Keyword stuffing, duplicate pages targeting slight keyword variations, hidden text, fake reviews or ratings, invented statistics, doorway pages, auto-generated content without review.

## Checks for this area

`npm run test:e2e` runs `tests/e2e/seo.spec.ts` over every built page (title, description, canonical, `lang`, single `h1`, image `alt`, valid JSON-LD). Use `.cursor/skills/seo-review/SKILL.md` for a manual audit.
